<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 256 0 R
/E (This matters for Bauchi specifically and concretely, and Chapter 05 is devoted to it in full, because the one thread of the fragmenting order the state most needs to change is the one that is changing least. These global shifts are not a backdrop against which Bauchi does its unglamorous fiscal work. They are transmission channels that have already reached the state, and whether they lift it or bury it will be decided by an institutional variable that has nothing to do with geopolitics and everything to do with tenement rating, remittance discipline, and contract negotiation. To see why, Chapter 02 sets out the structural framework that makes the terrain intelligible.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
