1155 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 285 0 R
/E (The dependency cycle follows directly: low IGR leads to high dependence on federal transfers, which yields limited fiscal autonomy, which permits only reduced development investment, which produces weak private-sector growth, which keeps the tax base narrow, which sustains low IGR. This is the rentier dynamic of Chapter 03, reproduced at the subnational scale: a government funded from the centre rather than by its own residents, and therefore under muted pressure to build the machinery that would tax them. )
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
